H4900.definition:
a primitive root;
to draw, used in a great variety of applications (including to sow, to sound, to prolong, to develop, to march, to remove, to delay, to be tall, etc.)
KJV: draw (along, out), continue, defer, extend, forbear, [idiom] give, handle, make (pro-, sound) long, [idiom] sow, scatter, stretch out.

H4901.definition:
from H4900 (מָשַׁךְ);
a sowing; also a possession
KJV: precious, price.

H4902.definition:
the same in form as H4901 (מֶשֶׁךְ), but probably of foreign derivation;
Meshek, a son of Japheth, and the people descended from him
KJV: Mesech, Meshech.

H4903.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H4904 (מִשְׁכָּב);
a bed
KJV: bed.

H4904.definition:
from H7901 (שָׁכַב);
a bed (figuratively, a bier); abstractly, sleep; by euphemism, carnal intercourse
KJV: bed(-chamber), couch, lieth (lying) with.

H4905.definition:
from H7919 (שָׂכַל);
instructive, i.e. a didactic poem
KJV: Maschil.

H4906.definition:
from the same as H7906 (שֵׂכוּ);
a figure (carved on stone, the wall, or any object); figuratively, imagination
KJV: conceit, image(-ry), picture, [idiom] wish.

H4907.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H4908 (מִשְׁכָּן);
residence
KJV: habitation.

H4908.definition:
from H7931 (שָׁכַן);
a residence (including a shepherd's hut, the lair of animals, figuratively, the grave; also the Temple); specifically, the Tabernacle (properly, its wooden walls)
KJV: dwelleth, dwelling (place), habitation, tabernacle, tent.

H4909.definition:
from H7936 (שָׂכַר);
wages or a reward
KJV: reward, wages.

H4910.definition:
a primitive root;
to rule
KJV: (have, make to have) dominion, governor, [idiom] indeed, reign, (bear, cause to, have) rule(-ing, -r), have power.

H4911.definition:
denominative from H4912 (מָשָׁל);
to liken, i.e. (transitively) to use figurative language (an allegory, adage, song or the like); intransitively, to resemble
KJV: be(-come) like, compare, use (as a) proverb, speak (in proverbs), utter.

H4912.definition:
apparently from H4910 (מָשַׁל) in some original sense of superiority in mental action;
properly, a pithy maxim, usually of metaphorical nature; hence, a simile (as an adage, poem, discourse)
KJV: byword, like, parable, proverb.

H4913.definition:
for H4861 (מִשְׁאָל);
Mashal, a place in Palestine
KJV: Mashal.

H4914.definition:
from H4911 (מָשַׁל);
a satire
KJV: byword.

H4915.definition:
(1) from H4910 (מָשַׁל); (2) from H4911 (מָשַׁל);
empire; a parallel
KJV: dominion, like.

H4916.definition:
or מִשְׁלֹחַ; also מִשְׁלָח; from H7971 (שָׁלַח);
a sending out, i.e. (abstractly) presentation (favorable), or seizure (unfavorable); also (concretely) a place of dismissal, or a business to be discharged
KJV: to lay, to put, sending (forth), to set.

H4917.definition:
feminine of H4916 (מִשְׁלוֹחַ);
a mission, i.e. (abstractly and favorable) release, or (concretely and unfavorable) an army
KJV: discharge, sending.

H4918.definition:
from H7999 (שָׁלַם); allied;
Meshullam, the name of seventeen Israelites
KJV: Meshullam.

H4920.definition:
or מְשֶׁלֶמְיָהוּ; from H7999 (שָׁלַם) and H3050 (יָהּ); ally of Jah;
Meshelemjah, an Israelite
KJV: Meshelemiah.

H4921.definition:
from H7999 (שָׁלַם); reconciliation;
Meshillemith, an Israelite
KJV: Meshillemith. Compare H4919 (מְשִׁלֵּמוֹת).

H4922.definition:
feminine of H4918 (מְשֻׁלָּם);
Meshullemeth, an Israelitess
KJV: Meshullemeth.

H4923.definition:
from H8074 (שָׁמֵם);
a waste or amazement
KJV: astonishment, desolate.

H4924.definition:
from H8080 (שָׁמַן);
fat, i.e. (literally and abstractly) fatness; but usually (figuratively and concretely) a rich dish, a fertile field, a robust man
KJV: fat (one, -ness, -test, -test place).

H4925.definition:
from H8080 (שָׁמַן); fatness;
Mashmannah, an Israelite
KJV: Mishmannah.

H4926.definition:
from H8085 (שָׁמַע);
a report
KJV: hearing.

H4927.definition:
the same as H4926 (מִשְׁמָע);
Mishma, the name of a son of Ishmael, and of an Israelite
KJV: Mishma.

H4928.definition:
feminine of H4926 (מִשְׁמָע);
audience, i.e. the royal court; also obedience, i.e. (concretely) a subject
KJV: bidding, guard, obey.

H4929.definition:
from H8104 (שָׁמַר);
a guard (the man, the post or the prison); a deposit (figuratively); also (as observed) a usage (abstractly), or an example (concretely)
KJV: diligence, guard, office, prison, ward, watch.

H4930.definition:
for H4548 (מַסְמֵר) fem.;
a peg
KJV: nail.

H4931.definition:
feminine of H4929 (מִשְׁמָר);
watch, i.e. the act (custody), or (concretely) the sentry, the post; objectively preservation, or (concretely) safe; figuratively observance, i.e. (abstractly) duty or (objectively) a usage or party
KJV: charge, keep, or to be kept, office, ordinace, safeguard, ward, watch.

H4932.definition:
from H8138 (שָׁנָה);
properly, a repetition, i.e. a duplicate (copy of a document), or a double (in amount); by implication, a second (in order, rank, age, quality or location)
KJV: college, copy, double, fatlings, next, second (order), twice as much.

H4933.definition:
from H8155 (שָׁסַס);
plunder
KJV: booty, spoil.

H4934.definition:
from the same as H8168 (שֹׁעַל);
a hollow, i.e. a narrow passage
KJV: path.

H4935.definition:
probably from H8159 (שָׁעָה);
inspection
KJV: to supple.

H4936.definition:
apparently from H8159 (שָׁעָה); inspection;
Misham, an Israelite
KJV: Misham.

H4937.definition:
or מִשְׁעָן; from H8172 (שָׁעַן);
a support (concretely), i.e. (figuratively) a protector or sustenance
KJV: stay.

H4938.definition:
or מִשְׁעֶנֶת; feminine of H4937 (מִשְׁעֵן);
support (abstractly), i.e. (figuratively) sustenance or (concretely) a walking-stick
KJV: staff.

H4940.definition:
from H8192 (שָׁפָה) (compare H8198 (שִׁפְחָה));
a family, i.e. circle of relatives; figuratively, a class (of persons), a species (of animals) or sort (of things); by extension a tribe or people
KJV: family, kind(-red).

H4941.definition:
from H8199 (שָׁפַט);
properly, a verdict (favorable or unfavorable) pronounced judicially, especially a sentence or formal decree (human or (participant's) divine law, individual or collective), including the act, the place, the suit, the crime, and the penalty; abstractly, justice, including a participant's right or privilege (statutory or customary), or even a style
KJV: [phrase] adversary, ceremony, charge, [idiom] crime, custom, desert, determination, discretion, disposing, due, fashion, form, to be judged, judgment, just(-ice, -ly), (manner of) law(-ful), manner, measure, (due) order, ordinance, right, sentence, usest, [idiom] worthy, [phrase] wrong.

H4942.definition:
from H8192 (שָׁפָה);
a stall for cattle (only dual)
KJV: burden, sheepfold.

H4943.definition:
from an unused root meaning to hold;
possession
KJV: [phrase] steward.

H4944.definition:
from H8264 (שָׁקַק);
a traversing, i.e. rapid motion
KJV: running to and fro.

H4945.definition:
from H8248 (שָׁקָה);
properly, causing to drink, i.e. a butler; by implication (intransitively), drink (itself); figuratively, a well-watered region
KJV: butler(-ship), cupbearer, drink(-ing), fat pasture, watered.

H4947.definition:
from H8259 (שָׁקַף) in its original sense of overhanging;
a lintel
KJV: lintel.

H4948.definition:
from H8254 (שָׁקַל);
weight (numerically estimated); hence, weighing (the act)
KJV: (full) weight.

H4949.definition:
or מִשְׁקֹלֶת; feminine of H4948 (מִשְׁקָל) or H4947 (מַשְׁקוֹף);
a weight, i.e. a plummet (with line attached)
KJV: plummet.

H4950.definition:
from H8257 (שָׁקַע);
a settling place (of water), i.e. a pond
KJV: deep.

H4952.definition:
from H8281 (שָׁרָה) in the sense of loosening;
maceration, i.e. steeped juice
KJV: liquor.

H4953.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H8319 (שָׁרַק);
a (musical) pipe (from its whistling sound)
KJV: flute.

H4954.definition:
patrial from an unused noun from an unused root; probably meaning to stretch out; extension;
a Mishraite, or inhabitant (collectively) of Mishra
KJV: Mishraites.

H4955.definition:
from H8313 (שָׂרַף);
combustion, i.e. cremation (of a corpse), or calcination (of lime)
KJV: burning.

H4956.definition:
from the plural of H4955 (מִשְׂרָפָה) and H4325 (מַיִם); burnings of water;
Misrephoth-Majim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Misrephoth-mayim.

H4957.definition:
a form for H7796 (שׂוֹרֵק) used denominatively; vineyard;
Masrekah, a place in Idumaea
KJV: Masrekah.

H4958.definition:
apparently from an unused root meaning to perforate, i.e. hollow out;
a pan
KJV: pan.

H4959.definition:
a primitive root;
to feel of; by implication, to grope
KJV: feel, grope, search.

H4960.definition:
from H8354 (שָׁתָה);
drink, by implication, drinking (the act); also (by implication) a banquet or (generally) feast
KJV: banquet, drank, drink, feast((-ed), -ing).

H4961.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H4960 (מִשְׁתֶּה);
a banquet
KJV: banquet.

H4962.definition:
from the same as H4970 (מָתַי);
properly, an adult (as of full length); by implication, a man (only in the plural)
KJV: [phrase] few, [idiom] friends, men, persons, [idiom] small.

H4963.definition:
denominative from H8401 (תֶּבֶן);
straw in the heap
KJV: straw.

H4964.definition:
from an unused root meaning to curb;
a bit
KJV: bit, bridle.

H4965.definition:
from H4964 (מֶתֶג) and H520 (אַמָּה) with the art. interposed; bit of the metropolis;
Metheg-ha-Ammah, an epithet of Gath
KJV: Metheg-ammah.

H4966.definition:
or מָתוּק; from H4985 (מָתַק);
sweet
KJV: sweet(-er, -ness).

H4967.definition:
from H4962 (מַת) and H410 (אֵל), with the relative interposed; man who (is) of God;
Methusael, an antediluvian patriarch
KJV: Methusael.

H4968.definition:
from H4962 (מַת) and H7973 (שֶׁלַח); man of a dart;
Methushelach, an antediluvian patriarch
KJV: Methuselah.

H4969.definition:
a primitive root;
to stretch out
KJV: spread out.

H4970.definition:
from an unused root meaning to extend;
properly, extent (of time); but used only adverbially (especially with other particle prefixes), when (either relative or interrogative)
KJV: long, when.

H4971.definition:
or מַתְכֻנֶת; from H8505 (תָּכַן) in the transferred sense of measuring;
proportion (in size, number or ingredients)
KJV: composition, measure, state, tale.

H4972.definition:
from H4100 (מָה) and H8513 (תְּלָאָה);
what a trouble!
KJV: what a weariness.

H4973.definition:
contr. from H3216 (יָלַע);
properly, a biter, i.e. a tooth
KJV: cheek (jaw) tooth, jaw.

H4974.definition:
from H8552 (תָּמַם);
wholesomeness; also (adverb) completely
KJV: men (by reading H4962 (מַת)), soundness.

H4975.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be slender;
properly, the waist or small of the back; only in plural the loins
KJV: [phrase] greyhound, loins, side.

H4976.definition:
from H5414 (נָתַן);
a present
KJV: gift, to give, reward.

H4977.definition:
the same as H4976 (מַתָּן);
Mattan, the name of a priest of Baal, and of an Israelite
KJV: Mattan.

H4978.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H4979 (מַתָּנָה)
{a present; specifically (in a good sense), a sacrificial offering, (in a bad sense) a bribe}
KJV: gift.

H4979.definition:
feminine of H4976 (מַתָּן);
a present; specifically (in a good sense), a sacrificial offering, (in a bad sense) a bribe
KJV: gift.

H4980.definition:
the same as H4979 (מַתָּנָה);
Mattanah, a place in the Desert
KJV: Mattanah.

H4981.definition:
probably patrial from an unused noun meaning slenderness;
a Mithnite, or inhabitant of Methen
KJV: Mithnite.

H4982.definition:
from H4976 (מַתָּן); liberal;
Mattenai, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Mattenai.

H4983.definition:
or מַתַּנְיָהוּ; from H4976 (מַתָּן) and H3050 (יָהּ); gift of Jah;
Mattanjah, the name of ten Israelites
KJV: Mattaniah.

H4984.definition:
from H5375 (נָשָׂא);
(used as abstractly) supreme exaltation
KJV: exalted.

H4985.definition:
a primitive root;
to suck, by implication, to relish, or (intransitively) be sweet
KJV: be (made, [idiom] take) sweet.

H4986.definition:
from H4985 (מָתַק);
figuratively, pleasantness (of discourse)
KJV: sweetness.

H4988.definition:
from H4985 (מָתַק);
a dainty, i.e. (generally) food
KJV: feed sweetly.

H4989.definition:
feminine of H4987 (מֹתֶק); sweetness;
Mithkah, a place in the Desert
KJV: Mithcah.

H4990.definition:
of Persian origin;
Mithredath, the name of two Persians
KJV: Mithredath.

H4991.definition:
feminine of H4976 (מַתָּן) abbreviated form;
a present
KJV: gift.

H4992.definition:
for H4993 (מַתִּתְיָה); gift of Jah;
Mattattah, an Israelite
KJV: Mattathah.

H4993.definition:
or מַתִּתְיָהוּ; from H4991 (מַתָּת) and H3050 (יָהּ); gift of Jah;
Mattithjah, the name of four Israelites
KJV: Mattithiah. n

H4994.definition:
a primitive particle of incitement and entreaty, which may usually be rendered;
'I pray', 'now', or 'then'; added mostly to verbs (in the Imperative or Future), or to interjections, occasionally to an adverb or conjunction
KJV: I beseech (pray) thee (you), go to, now, oh.

H4995.definition:
apparently from H5106 (נוּא) in the sense of harshness from refusal;
properly, tough, i.e. uncooked (flesh)
KJV: raw.

H4996.definition:
of Egyptian origin;
No (i.e. Thebes), the capital of Upper Egypt
KJV: No. Compare H528 (אָמוֹן).

H4997.definition:
or נאוֹדlemma נֹאוד vowel, corrected to נאוֹדxlit nôʼwd corrected to nʼôwd; also (feminine) נֹאדָה; from an unused root of uncertain signification;
a (skin or leather) bag (for fluids)
KJV: bottle.

H4998.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to be at home, i.e. (by implication) to be pleasant (or suitable), i.e. beautiful
KJV: be beautiful, become, be comely.

H4999.definition:
from H4998 (נָאָה);
a home; figuratively, a pasture
KJV: habitation, house, pasture, pleasant place.
